  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-116333",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL parallel B-tree array scan reads beyond array bounds",
  "details": "Buffer over-read in PostgreSQL parallel B-tree scans allows an object creator to read attacker-chosen server-memory addresses, via a function incorrectly marked PARALLEL SAFE or STABLE to make participating workers build different scan-key arrays.  Within major versions 17-18, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.7 and 17.12 are affected.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17 are unaffected.",
